Now Slider and Stepper — binding-first `.of(binding, min, max[, step])`, initial value from `binding.get()`. The render currently uses `value` field. With binding-first, the `value` field becomes `binding.get()` at render time. Let me update Slider to read value from binding.

Current Slider.render:
```
node.properties.put(Properties.VALUE, value);
node.properties.put(Properties.MIN_VALUE, min);
node.properties.put(Properties.MAX_VALUE, max);
node.propertyBindings.put(Properties.VALUE, binding);
node.valueInput = binding::set;
```

With binding-first, I'll keep `min`, `max`, `binding` fields, and set VALUE = binding.get(). Let me rewrite Slider.

