This is a large mechanical rewrite of the sugar methods. Given ~60 methods, doing this via Edit tool method-by-method would be very slow. A Python script that rewrites each `return Modified.props(...)` body to `return modifier(X.of(...))` is more efficient. But the mapping from each method to its modifier class + `.of(...)` args is specific. Let me do a targeted Python transform.

Approach: I'll rewrite the whole "Global modifiers" section of View.java programmatically. Actually, it might be cleaner to write a Python script that processes View.java and, for each known sugar method, replaces the body. But matching multi-line bodies via regex is error-prone.

Alternative: Since I know the exact current bodies (from reading View.java earlier), I can do surgical Edit calls per method — but that's ~60 edits.

Better: Use a Python script with explicit (old_text → new_text) replacements for each method body. The old bodies are unique enough (they contain distinct `Modified.prop(Properties.X, ...)`).

